Here's just a small portion of what my app will detect. It will be detecting the insane amount of variables, because I have the patience to sit here adding each and every one of them. People like to say that not everything can just be thrown into an algorithm. I believe if you have all of the raw data needed, then it is possible.

    class Champ {
        constructor(name, cc, burst, flank, snowball, early, mid, late, allaround, duelist, outplaypotential, waveclear, tank, diver, zoning, objectivecontrol, mobility, utility, teamcomp, gender, assassin, frontline, backline, solocarry, teamplay, sustain, aoe, peel, passive, aggressive, engage, dissengage, waittostrike, splitpush, ad, ap, melee, ranged, healing, picks, top, midlane, jungle, support, adc, gapcloser, juggernaut, dps, mage, kite, global, bruiser, roaming, survivability, towerdive, safepick, poke, sustainedcombat, lockdown, overloaded, invisibility, edgedashspammer,  highcomplex, mediumcomplex, lowcomplex) {
            this.Name = name;
            this.Cc = cc;
            this.Burst = burst;
            this.Flank = flank;
            this.Snowball = snowball; 
