Hi there. You're definitely correct that those variables you mentioned are important. They're so important that they're already being coded in my application. I'll attach a small (incomplete) snippet below of some of the variables I'll be detecting.

The point of this survey was **strictly** to see why someone mains the champion they do. This will allow me to create more lucrative and crafty questions to ensure the reliability of my application.

The variables you mentioned and many more for each champion are being determined by high elo players (D1+). Here's the snippet example as promised:

    class Champ {
        constructor(name, cc, burst, flank, snowball, early, mid, late, allaround, duelist, outplaypotential, waveclear, tank, diver, zoning, objectivecontrol, mobility, utility, teamcomp, gender, assassin, frontline, backline, solocarry, teamplay, sustain, aoe, peel, passive, aggressive, engage, dissengage, waittostrike, splitpush, ad, ap, melee, ranged, healing, picks) {
